\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Left: the selection funnel. The three denominators the text keeps apart are the catalogued population, the 168-entry ALMA-covered work list, the ${\sim }115$ stars a public field genuinely contains, and the 94{} searched. Right: the decision flow from spectral window to disposition. The 512-control comparison is a candidate-generation screen, and the gates in italic are where a crossing can leave the chain. The whole chain in one line: 1655{} windows $\rightarrow $ 75{} threshold crossings $\rightarrow $ 13{} stage-1 spatial outliers $\rightarrow $ 9{} attributed to molecular emission $\rightarrow $ 4{} unattributed, against 3.2{} expected by chance $\rightarrow $ 0{} persistent, independently confirmed technosignatures.}}{5}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:funnel}{{2}{5}{Left: the selection funnel. The three denominators the text keeps apart are the catalogued population, the \NCensus -entry ALMA-covered work list, the ${\sim }\NGenuinelyCovered $ stars a public field genuinely contains, and the \NStars {} searched. Right: the decision flow from spectral window to disposition. The \NCtrl -control comparison is a candidate-generation screen, and the gates in italic are where a crossing can leave the chain. The whole chain in one line: \NWindows {} windows $\rightarrow $ \NHits {} threshold crossings $\rightarrow $ \NStageOneWin {} stage-1 spatial outliers $\rightarrow $ \NStageOneLine {} attributed to molecular emission $\rightarrow $ \NStageOneUnattrib {} unattributed, against \ExpStageOneAll {} expected by chance $\rightarrow $ \NCandidates {} persistent, independently confirmed technosignatures}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Where this survey searched. \emph  {Lower panel:} each searched window is a horizontal segment on its host system's row, rows ordered by distance and labelled alternately on the left and right axes; heavy blue marks the fine-channel carrier search (Class\nobreakspace  {}A) and light grey the unresolved spectral excess search (Class\nobreakspace  {}B). \emph  {Upper panel:} the number of systems covering each gigahertz of sky frequency. The panel shows coverage and search class only; the threshold distribution is Fig.\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:context}. The coverage is narrow, clustered and repeatedly revisited: 46{} islands concentrated near 230 and 345\,GHz, with summed window bandwidth $24.0\times $ the union. The union is the frequency coverage; the summed bandwidth is the integrated search effort, and the two answer different questions (Scope of the constraints, \S  \ref  {sec:method}).}}{5}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:waterfall}{{3}{5}{Where this survey searched. \emph {Lower panel:} each searched window is a horizontal segment on its host system's row, rows ordered by distance and labelled alternately on the left and right axes; heavy blue marks the fine-channel carrier search (Class~A) and light grey the unresolved spectral excess search (Class~B). \emph {Upper panel:} the number of systems covering each gigahertz of sky frequency. The panel shows coverage and search class only; the threshold distribution is Fig.~\ref {fig:context}. The coverage is narrow, clustered and repeatedly revisited: \UnionIntervals {} islands concentrated near 230 and 345\,GHz, with summed window bandwidth $\GrossOverUnion \times $ the union. The union is the frequency coverage; the summed bandwidth is the integrated search effort, and the two answer different questions (Scope of the constraints, \S \ref {sec:method})}{figure.3}{}}
